@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. GET all courses — expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses


### 2. GET one existing course — expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/2


### 3. GET a nonexistent course — expect 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/999


### 4. GET user 1's completed courses — expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/completions


### 5. POST invalid course — expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": "CSC4600",
  "credits": 3,
  "description": "Missing title",
  "prerequisites": []
}


### 6. POST valid course — expect 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": "CSC4600",
  "title": "Cloud Computing",
  "credits": 3,
  "description": "Test course",
  "prerequisites": [5, 9]
}


### 7.  DELETE
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/courses/13


### 8. PUT valid completions — expect 200 OK
PUT {{baseUrl}}/completions
Content-Type: application/json

[1, 3, 7]


### 9. PUT invalid completions — expect 400 Bad Request
# Course 2 requires course 1, which is missing
PUT {{baseUrl}}/completions
Content-Type: application/json

[2]


### 10. GET completions after invalid PUT — expect 200 OK
# Verify the invalid request did not change saved data
GET {{baseUrl}}/completions


### Restore original sample completions — expect 200 OK
PUT {{baseUrl}}/completions
Content-Type: application/json

[1, 3]